WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.109 --> 00:00:04.828
On the last day of camp, the air buzzed with excitement.

2
00:00:04.829 --> 00:00:13.032
Iris dropped off her lunch and hurried to join Grace and the other girls at the courts.

3
00:00:13.033 --> 00:00:16.174
She was ready to play tennis!

4
00:00:16.175 --> 00:00:24.274
Until something strange caught her attention. Javier was striding toward Jae.

5
00:00:24.275 --> 00:00:30.924
He muttered something to Jae and then beckoned him over to a secluded spot near a pine tree.

6
00:00:30.925 --> 00:00:38.279
"What's going on?" Iris thought. She moved closer to the boys.

7
00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:45.836
"I know what you tried with my sister, and I don't like it," Javier snapped, scowling.

8
00:00:45.837 --> 00:00:50.174
"Wha-what are you talking about?" Jae stammered.

9
00:00:50.175 --> 00:00:57.862
"You were trying to convince her to join the older kids' group so you could laugh at her," Javier said.

10
00:00:57.864 --> 00:01:01.407
"I heard you and Zoe talking about it."

11
00:01:01.408 --> 00:01:08.059
Iris' face flamed. That was why Jae had suggested they could be doubles partners?

12
00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:14.056
"Dude, I was just goofing around." Jae let out a feeble laugh.

13
00:01:14.057 --> 00:01:24.138
"Besides, it was Zoe's idea. Zoe thinks your sister likes me, so she told me to say that to Iris to see what would happen."

14
00:01:24.139 --> 00:01:30.287
Javier raised his voice. "Leave Iris alone. Got it?"

15
00:01:30.288 --> 00:01:32.814
"Yeah, man, whatever."

16
00:01:32.815 --> 00:01:44.794
They broke apart, and Iris ducked behind a tree as the boys walked by. Javier had been trying to protect her from Jae!

17
00:01:44.795 --> 00:01:50.969
That helped Iris to feel a little better. But still . . . Jae didn't like her.

18
00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:56.943
He'd only been making fun of her—and she had almost fallen for it!

19
00:01:56.944 --> 00:02:05.039
"Focus," a voice inside Iris commanded. She'd played enough soccer games to know how to compete mentally.

20
00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:09.001
"Stop thinking about Jae, and think about your game."

21
00:02:09.002 --> 00:02:16.590
Ally had basically told Iris the same thing: when you're playing tennis, you have to think about tennis.

22
00:02:16.591 --> 00:02:24.074
Iris inhaled deeply and raced over to join her group.

23
00:02:24.075 --> 00:02:31.020
"Hi, everyone!" Ally was beaming. "It's time to announce final partners and matchups."

24
00:02:31.021 --> 00:02:35.825
Everyone cheered, including Iris.

25
00:02:35.826 --> 00:02:41.840
"We'll start with Anna and Kaylee against Alex and Oliver," Ally went on.

26
00:02:41.841 --> 00:02:52.740
"And next Risa and Natalie against Akira and Aiden, and the final matchup will be Iris and Grace against Javier and Ben.

27
00:02:52.741 --> 00:03:00.334
Anyway, we'll play after lunch. For now, we get to watch the older kids play."

28
00:03:00.335 --> 00:03:12.388
During the morning's matches, Iris paid close attention, carefully noting the older kids' skills—the way they returned the ball and looked for opportunities to score points.

29
00:03:12.389 --> 00:03:17.061
But she could barely watch when Jae played doubles with Zoe.

30
00:03:17.062 --> 00:03:23.035
When they won, they grinned and high-fived as if they'd just won Wimbledon.

31
00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:26.709
How could she have once thought that Jae was nice?

32
00:03:26.710 --> 00:03:32.624
Grace did some last-minute coaching of Iris, Anna, and Risa during lunch.

33
00:03:32.625 --> 00:03:40.704
"Remember, the boys will try to hit to you three newbies as often as possible. But you guys are ready."

34
00:03:40.705 --> 00:03:44.518
"Let's go!" Ally called.

35
00:03:44.519 --> 00:03:49.857
Julie, the camp director, signaled the first players into position.

36
00:03:49.858 --> 00:03:58.198
Anna and Kaylee won their match against Alex and Oliver, but Akira and Aiden beat Risa and Natalie.

37
00:03:58.199 --> 00:04:03.660
It was up to Iris and Grace to put the final win in the girls' column.

38
00:04:03.661 --> 00:04:07.097
Iris looked across the net at her brother.

39
00:04:07.098 --> 00:04:14.819
She still wanted to do her best, but her strong desire to beat Javier had disappeared.

40
00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:20.265
Ben served the ball. It rocketed right at Iris.

41
00:04:20.266 --> 00:04:27.812
Standing with her feet hip-width apart, she kept her eyes on the ball and batted it right back.

42
00:04:27.813 --> 00:04:33.074
Before either boy reached the ball, it landed with a thud.

43
00:04:33.075 --> 00:04:36.982
"Love–fifteen!" Julie called.

44
00:04:36.983 --> 00:04:43.085
"Whoa!" Iris' mouth dropped open. She had scored the first point!

45
00:04:43.086 --> 00:04:50.813
Along the sideline, people fist-bumped, reminding Iris that fans weren't supposed to cheer loudly like in soccer.

46
00:04:50.814 --> 00:04:59.611
She wondered if Jae was watching her. But before she could find him in the crowd, Ben served straight to her again.

47
00:04:59.612 --> 00:05:09.805
She swung but only managed to tip the ball with her racket. The ball crashed down to her feet.

48
00:05:09.806 --> 00:05:14.629
"Fifteen all!" The score was tied.

49
00:05:14.630 --> 00:05:23.862
The games, and then the sets, went on, with the lead flipping back and forth between the girls' and boys' teams.

50
00:05:23.863 --> 00:05:32.528
One point for Iris' team, and then one for Javier's, until they were on the seventh game of the third set.

51
00:05:32.529 --> 00:05:40.498
Sweat dripped down Iris' neck. It was down to the last point, and it was Javier's turn to serve.

52
00:05:40.499 --> 00:05:45.172
Javier tossed the ball into the air and swung.

53
00:05:45.173 --> 00:05:53.831
The ball landed closer to Iris than to Grace. Iris knew she could win the game with one well-executed fake.

54
00:05:53.832 --> 00:05:58.156
Her eyes flicked toward Javier. He was her brother.

55
00:05:58.157 --> 00:06:06.412
Her annoying sloth of a brother. The same brother who had gotten furious at Jae for being mean to her.

56
00:06:06.413 --> 00:06:10.530
For a millisecond she was tempted to let him win.

57
00:06:10.531 --> 00:06:18.639
But she was a competitive athlete and a good teammate, so instead Iris dove for the ball.

58
00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:31.567
She twisted her body for the fake. The ball sailed over the net toward Javier, who missed it.

59
00:06:31.568 --> 00:06:35.888
"Game, set, match!" Ally called.

60
00:06:35.889 --> 00:06:39.893
Iris and Grace raised their rackets in victory.

61
00:06:39.894 --> 00:06:49.633
Disappointment filled Ben's face. Javier's too. "Good game, girls," the boys said, stepping toward the net to shake hands.

62
00:06:49.634 --> 00:06:55.400
Iris approached her brother. "I heard what you said, Javier."

63
00:06:55.401 --> 00:06:57.382
"What are you talking about?"

64
00:06:57.383 --> 00:07:02.372
"To Jae." Iris looked her brother in the eye. "Thank you."

65
00:07:02.373 --> 00:07:08.616
"Oh, that." Javier shrugged. "You're welcome. He's a jerk."

66
00:07:08.617 --> 00:07:16.504
Iris nodded as she shook her brother's hand. "We completely agree on that, bro!"

67
00:07:16.505 --> 00:07:26.117
"How did it go today?" Mama called from the kitchen. She'd come home from work a bit early and was frying something on the stovetop.

68
00:07:26.118 --> 00:07:30.868
Iris followed Javier down the hall.

69
00:07:30.869 --> 00:07:35.182
"Steak!" he announced.

70
00:07:35.183 --> 00:07:41.181
Iris couldn't remember the last time they'd had steak. Her mouth watered.

71
00:07:41.182 --> 00:07:51.016
Javier smiled at Mama, and Mama smiled back at both of them. Then she set the steak on a cutting board and waved at the table.

72
00:07:51.017 --> 00:07:55.712
"Come and sit, and tell me all about the last day of camp."

73
00:07:55.713 --> 00:07:59.835
"Iris won the final match," Javier said.

74
00:07:59.836 --> 00:08:11.127
"But Javier's team almost beat us," Iris said quickly. "It was a close game, and he really improved a lot. We both did, in fact."

75
00:08:11.128 --> 00:08:16.034
"Sounds like it was a good experience for both of you then," Mama said.

76
00:08:16.035 --> 00:08:17.968
They nodded.

77
00:08:17.969 --> 00:08:26.379
"Good," Mama said. "Because summer is not over yet. And I signed you up for another camp."

78
00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:30.075
"Huh?" Iris looked at Mama in surprise.

79
00:08:30.076 --> 00:08:35.540
"It was the only camp that still had openings," Mama went on.

80
00:08:35.541 --> 00:08:39.447
"And you'll be happy to know it's not tennis camp."

81
00:08:39.448 --> 00:08:43.525
"What is it?" Javier sighed.

82
00:08:43.526 --> 00:08:47.354
Mama smiled. "Math camp."

83
00:08:47.355 --> 00:08:54.861
Math camp? Iris and Javier looked at each other and burst out laughing.

84
00:08:54.862 --> 00:09:02.013
One thing was sure: if they'd survived tennis camp, they could survive anything.

85
00:09:02.014 --> 00:09:09.229
Even math camp.

